{{also|éloquent}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{term|eloquens||speaking, having the faculty of speech, eloquent}}, ppr. of {{term|eloqui||to speak out}} < {{term|e||out}} + {{term|loqui||to speak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɛl.əˌkwənt/}} {{SAMPA|/"El.@%kw@nt/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more}}

# [[fluently]] [[persuasive]] and [[articulate]]
# [[effective]] in [[expressing]] [[meaning]] by [[speech]]

====Usage notes====
'''Eloquent''' expresses stronger praise than do {{term|articulate}} or {{term|well-spoken}}.

